CHANGELOG.md:256:- **B-70e9** (unify host-side LLM usage capture): added `lattice host_run`, a single launcher choke point (`packages/main/src/core/host-run.ts` + `handlers/host-run.ts`) that runs a canonical reviewer/quorum host (codex/claude/agy) via the B-d8ef canonical launcher argv, streams host stdout live, and writes preflight + final usage-ledger rows bound to storyId/agentType/phase/provider (plus reviewRunId->threadId and lane->subagentId). Provider truth over estimates: codex maps the `turn.completed` usage event (uncached input remainder + cacheRead), claude maps the stream-json `result` usage, and agy records `source=unavailable` because its print mode exposes no usage. Fail-closed caps run BEFORE spawn — the per-dispatch hard-budget cap (`LATTICE_HARD_BUDGET_TOKENS`) and a host-run concurrency cap (`LATTICE_HOST_RUN_MAX_CONCURRENT`, default 4; stale slots reclaimed via `LATTICE_HOST_RUN_SLOT_STALE_MS`, default 6h; no queuing) — and each refusal is recorded as a blocked ledger row. The same seam now also covers the autopilot repair step, the host-readiness probes, and the cross-host-review codex leaf so those runs are no longer invisible in the ledger. Added `lattice usage_sweep`, a strictly read-only retro-attribution sweep over `~/.codex/sessions` rollouts and `~/.claude/projects` transcripts that emits a NON-AUTHORITATIVE token-attribution estimate only (no ledger backfill, no gate evidence). Usage rows stay `gateEvidence=false` diagnostics and never gate the workflow. New docs page `docs/host-run-usage.md`; new smokes `host-run-usage-smoke` + `usage-sweep-smoke` wired as `test:host-run-usage` / `test:usage-sweep`.
